libcamera: software_isp: validate autofocus controls from applications

The autofocus algorithm reads the AF controls of a request with the typed
ControlList::get(), which asserts that the value has the type the control
declares and, for a scalar control, that it does not hold an array. A client
that writes a one-element AfWindows as a scalar Rectangle, as libcamera-rs
does, trips the assert and aborts the whole camera process instead of failing
that request. Check the type and the array flag of the raw value before the
typed get, accept a scalar rectangle as a list of one window, and ignore a
malformed value with a warning so that autofocus keeps its previous state.

---
